    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Split your data into training and test sets.\r\n- Scale your data if necessary.\r\n- Fit your model.\r\n- In your Project Planning Guide, respond to the question in **Step 5: Modeling**, under **Splitting, Scaling, and Fitting**.\r\n\r\n💻 Coding Tip\r\n\r\nRecall that you can use `train_test_split` to split your data into training and test sets.\r\n\r\n```\r\ntrain_inputs, test_inputs, train_outputs, test_outputs = train_test_split(\r\n    inputs, outputs, test_size=0.25\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso recall that you can use `MinMaxScaler` to scale your training and test inputs.\r\n\r\n```\r\nscaler = MinMaxScaler()\r\nscaled_train_inputs = scaler.fit_transform(train_inputs)\r\nscaled_test_inputs = scaler.transform(test_inputs)\r\n```\r\n",
